        <!--
          ⚠️ This rule was declared between pair_0 and pair_1, while `render` has always drawn it
          with `rule(rule_6, before = pairShown, after = footShown)` — the separator between the
          two-column block and the footer. So the hairline appeared in the MIDDLE of the columns,
          the footer had none above it, and neither was a compile error or a crash: a line in the
          wrong place is only ever visible on a phone. The id is unchanged, so nothing that names
          it has to move with it.
        -->
        <ImageView
            android:id="@+id/widget_board_rule_6"
            style="@style/WidgetBoardRule" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_board_foot"
            style="@style/WidgetLine.Board.Dim" />

        <!--
          ⚠️ The board could not say a feed had failed. `degradedLine` was folded only into the ROW
          list, so on BOTH tall sizes — the ones this board exists for — a dead source reported
          nothing at all and simply looked like a quiet day.

          It is its own view rather than part of the footer because the footer draws only on the
          full size, and a failure notice that appears at one height and not the other is half a
          diagnostic. This one draws whenever there is something to say, at every size, and is
          invisible the rest of the time.
        -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_board_degraded"
            style="@style/WidgetLine.Board.Degraded" />
